description:
The adjoint recursively reverses each qif arm while retaining forward arm order. ISA 0.9 section 5.3 K29 instead requires inversion of the complete expansion because allocations/releases are unconditional and may span arms. The legal identity action qif p { d=qalloc any 1 } { qfree d } runs forward, but its adjoint attempts qfree d before d exists. Expected identity on t=0,p=0; actual exit 1, unknown wire bundle d in @main. This also breaks CC/R reversal of an action containing this pattern.

Reviewed SHA: bda07e1af5d003f36fb8345487d9f9e5cce2d35b. Determining location: src/action.rs:2024.
Repro (headless task-local environment as in review): timeout 30s /home/tobias/Projects/bennett-workspace/bennett-vm/.tmp/rev-vm/target/debug/bennett-vm run-action /home/tobias/Projects/bennett-workspace/bennett-vm/.tmp/rev-vm/cross-arm.bisa main --mut 0 --in 0 --adjoint
Source (generated signatures/hashes are in the fixture):
action @main (t:wire mut) (p:wire in) () () ()
^e():
qif p {
d = qalloc any 1
} {
qfree d
}

Review only; no source fixes made.

P2 only under review policy rule 4: malformed request validation outside the ladder route; no demonstrated wrong result on a rung, oracle verdict, build or gate failure.

1. src/ref_library/oracle_source.rs:90-94: lower_oracle_with_token_aliases binds every decoded token to Value::TokenId, then validates only Value::Token. The budget validation loop is now dead for all token arguments. A memoryless oracle @o (x:wire in) (t:wire) (f:wire[4]) () (tk:token), body lift.retval x, accepts params [["1","1","0","0"]], primary context {"token":["1","0","0","0"]}, token_aliases [0,1]. The unused argument's heap=1 violates section 5.4. A stdin Rust probe linked to the reviewed library asserted validate_budget rejects it, then lower_oracle_with_token_aliases returned Ok with 488 leaves. The main-side code validates Value::Token before any identity conversion and would reject this request. Validate before binding or include TokenId in the pattern; add a negative library-level test. Repro source and command are below.

2. Formatting drift remains the previously filed bennett-vm-cak; timeout 30s cargo fmt --all -- --check exits 1 at reviewed head 5ea5dcb0a24fd2a132640a44caad39cf34507476. Formatting is not in gate.toml and is P2 per the review brief.

Other acknowledged deferred quality items remain owned by bennett-vm-bsj, bennett-vm-68j, bennett-vm-bai and bennett-vm-dhx; no additional blocking finding is asserted.

